    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Joining the events"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "To put events in order: **primero**, **luego**, **después**, **más tarde**, **al final**.\n\nTo give the reason, **porque** comes after the result: llegué tarde **porque** perdí el autobús.\n\nTo give the result, **por eso** comes after the reason: perdí el autobús, **por eso** llegué tarde.\n\nTo add: **además**. To contrast: **pero**.\n\nTo comment: **por suerte**, **por desgracia**.\n\nThe events themselves are in the **indefinido**. A connector at the start of the sentence is usually followed by a comma."
      }
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "titulo": {"en": "A bad day"},
      "frases": [
